 "notes": [
  "Source PDF lists members under two headings: 'EAST BENGAL' (78 numbered seats, numbered NE-1..NE-78) and 'WEST PAKISTAN-78' (78 numbered seats, numbered NW-1..NW-78), followed by a 'CHANGES MEMBERS FIRST CONSTITUTE ASSEMBLY FROM FEBRUARY 1966-1968' section listing 10 by-election replacements grouped by month (Feb 1966, Aug 1966, Mar 1967, Oct 1967) plus 'JULY, 1968 NIL'.",
  "Women's reserved seats: 3 under East Bengal heading (NE-76 'Women's Constituency-I', NE-77 'Women's Constituency-II', NE-78 'Women's Constituency-III') and 3 under West Pakistan heading (NW-76, NW-77, NW-78, same heading wording). All 6 tagged seat_type=reserved_women, elected_via=indirect per task instructions (1965 Basic Democrats electoral college era).",
  "All non-women's seats were also elected indirectly by the Basic Democracies electoral college in 1965, but per task instructions elected_via is left as 'general' for those (the 'indirect' tag is reserved for the women's-seat heading).",
  "Item numbered '48' in the East Bengal list is missing/blank in the source PDF text extraction (OCR dropped the row between items 47 and 49) -- no member could be transcribed for that row; not included in output.",
  "Two West Pakistan seats are marked 'Vacant' in the PDF at time of printing: NW-33 (Lyallpur-IV) and NW-4 (Karachi-cum-Lasbela). Neither is included as a member row. NW-4 was later filled by Mir Ghause Baksh per the Changes section (Feb 1966).",
  "Province field: East Bengal section mapped to 'East Pakistan'. West Pakistan section members are left province=null because the PDF only labels them 'WEST PAKISTAN' (the single 'One Unit' province in 1965); the schema's province enum has no 'West Pakistan' / single-unit option and inferring modern provinces from constituency city names was avoided to not invent data not stated by the PDF.",
  "Several constituency codes are duplicated across rows in the raw PDF text (e.g. NE-23 appears for both 'Bakerganj-V' item 37 and 'Bakerganj-IV' item 43; NE-65 for both 'Sylhet-I' item 45 and 'Comilla-V' item 51; NE-21/NE-20/NE-19 all labelled 'Bakerganj-II'; NW-34 appears for both 'Lyallpur-V' and 'Muzaffargarh-I'; NW-58 for both 'Montgomery-III' and 'Montgomery-II'; NW-66 for both 'Nawab Shah' and 'Quetta'; NW-74 appears three times for 'Sanghar-cum-Tharparkar' and 'Thatta'; NW-15 duplicates NW-14's 'Hazara-II' label). These are transcribed exactly as printed/OCR'd without correction, per instructions.",
  "OCR mangling of the type 'Wom en s' / 'Mohamm ad' with stray internal spaces was collapsed to normal spelling (e.g. 'Women's', 'Mohammad') per task instructions; no other spelling changes were made.",
  "Total rows transcribed: 77 East Bengal members (78 numbered, 1 blank/missing) + 3 East Bengal women's seats + 76 West Pakistan members (78 numbered minus 2 marked Vacant) + 3 West Pakistan women's seats + 10 by-election replacement members from the Changes section = 169 member records."
 ],
